# ress.sh — a redirector, and nothing else.
#
# There is no storage here, no account, and no copy of anyone's profile. A
# ress.sh link is a shorter way to write a GitHub URL, and `ress apply` resolves
# it locally before it makes any request at all.

/gh/*         https://github.com/:splat                                                      302
/repo         https://github.com/tsouth89/omarchy-resurrect                                  302
